{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["<b>And Jacob gave to Esau.</b> To acquire through the act of exchange, using the stew or the vessel containing the stew — after the manner of וְזֹאת לִפְנִים בְּיִשְׂרָאֵל עַל הַגְּאֻלָּה וְעַל הַתְּמוּרָה לְקַיֵּם כֹּל: שָׁלַף אִישׁ נַעֲלוֹ וְנָתַן לְרֵעֵהוּ (Ruth 4:7)." "<b>And Esau despised the birthright.</b> Even after the transaction, the birthright was in his eyes not worth the price they had agreed upon. Thus it is clear that the seller was not wronged, since the sale was not worth that much to him in the first place."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:31:47.277571431Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}